.TH SYSSCOPE-GLASSHOUSE 8 "2026-11-15" "sysscope 0.0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sysscope-glasshouse \- helper that runs a program in the Glasshouse sandbox
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysscope-glasshouse availability
.br
.B sysscope-glasshouse run-local
[\fB\-\-calibrate\fR] \fIFILE\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The helper started by
.BR sysscoped (8)
for each Glasshouse run. It prepares a run directory with decoy files, starts
the sample in a bubblewrap sandbox (new namespaces, no network but loopback,
seccomp filters, no capabilities, as the unprivileged user \fBsysscope-box\fR)
inside a systemd transient unit, and compares the decoys before and after.
Users run Glasshouse through \fBsysscope glasshouse run\fR or the GUI, not
through this program.
.PP
Glasshouse is a behaviour-demonstration sandbox, not a malware containment
system. For real or suspected malware use a separate virtual machine
(docs/REAL_SAMPLES.md).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B availability
Whether a sandbox can start on this system, and why not.
.TP
.B run-local
Run a sample without the daemon (testing; \fB\-\-calibrate\fR traces it with strace).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sysscope (1),
.BR sysscoped (8)
